  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday morning through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 230 PM EDT Thu May 14 2026\n\nLong term will mostly be focused on the dry conditions with warming \ntemperatures into the weekend and next week. Bermuda high settles \nback into the area into the weekend which will limit any approaching \nfronts to well north of our area. Shortwave pushes into far north \nGeorgia on Sunday but with a deep layer of dry air, rainfall is not \nexpected to occur. As the ridging settles in temperatures will begin \ntheir warming trend with highs in the mid to upper 80s across the \narea each day next week with portions of far southeastern central \nGeorgia potentially reaching near 90 degrees. Lows expected to only \ndip down into the mid to upper 60s most nights as well with \ntemperatures as a whole 7-12 degrees above normal. Towards the end \nof the longterm, there is an indication that a front will push into \nthe area bringing in rainfall Wednesday into Thursday IF the front \nis able to hold together. Overall the 6-10 and 8-14 day outlooks are \nindicating a return to above normal rainfall and above normal\ntemps.",
